{
  "_about": [
    "The panel lane, as worked cases (#151, #189 U-09; spec 2026-09-23-flows-mosaic-target-block-design.md 1.4 and 1.5).",
    "Every expectation was written from the spec's table and grammar, never generated by the code it grades.",
    "Graded by server/tests/test_flows_panel_lane.py (Python) and by the TypeScript mirror of owner_of / the lane (S3-U).",
    "owners: every lane node (AUTOFOCUS, GUIDE, legacy SLEW, CAPTURE LOOP, FILTER CYCLE) -> the id owner_of returns, or null.",
    "lanes: per TARGET/POOL id -> lane (ids by distance from the block, then canvas x, y, id), tail (null when the lane is empty or branched), branched, loop (a pass wire from the tail into the block's next exists), next (what the tail's flow output feeds, canvas order).",
    "compile: Python only. steps = the stage node ids each block's compiled entry carries, in order; notes = the stage node ids the compile names because the canvas-order rule would have assigned them differently.",
    "Port ids are matched as strings, so these graphs use 'pass' and 'next' whether or not the node vocabulary declares them yet."
  ],
